         Head of Digital's Computer Systems Division Resigns

MAYNARD, Mass., July 1, 1996 - Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced that Enrico Pesatori, vice president and general manager 
of the company's Computer Systems Division, has resigned from the 
company, effective immediately.

     Digital Chairman Robert B. Palmer will personally serve as the 
acting head of the Computer Systems Division which is made up of the 
company's System Business Unit and Personal Computer Business Unit, 
as well as Digital's operations in Europe and the Asia Pacific 
region.

     In announcing Pesatori's departure, Palmer said, "We recognize 
Enrico's significant contributions to Digital during a very 
difficult transition period and wish him well in his future 
endeavors." 

     Pesatori joined Digital in February, 1993, from Zenith Data 
Systems. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
