      Digital's Alpha Emerges as Premier NT Development Platform 
               at Bann as Companies Expand Partnership 

  Companies Unveil Mutually Sponsored Cooperative Technology Center   

Maynard, Mass, July 1, 1996 - Digital Equipment Corporation and The 
Baan Company today announced they will collaborate on a broad range 
of technology initiatives designed to deliver comprehensive software 
solutions and services to customers worldwide.

In addition, the two companies have also unveiled a mutually 
sponsored Cooperative Technology Center located at Baan's facility 
in Barneveld, Holland. The new Cooperative Technology Center is 
staffed by engineers from both Digital and Baan who are engaged in 
work that maximizes performance across the Digital Alpha and 
Intel-based computing environment. 

The core of the new Digital/Baan Cooperative Technology Center 
consists of Digital's high-performance 64-bit AlphaServer RISC 
systems. The Center is equipped with a Digital AlphaServer 8400 
system in addition to several AlphaServer 2100 systems. 

Through benchmarking and testing, Baan and Digital has achieved 
impressive performance engineering results ranging from 50 to 2000 
active users across the full line of Digital AlphaServer platforms. 
The Cooperative Technology Center is currently benchmarking larger 
systems and clusters for both UNIX and NT environments.

Baan, a company that has traditionally developed its suite of 
industry-leading Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) software 
solutions in the UNIX environment, worked first with Digital to 
cooperatively optimize its Windows NT development environment on  
Digital's AlphaServer platforms. Digital's Alpha and Intel 
technology running NT, and Alpha running Digital UNIX, are all 
strategic platforms for Baan development and deployment. These 
platforms are available at first release of Baan IV, an information 
technology system that integrates data captured from across all of 
the different stages of the supply chain.

In addition to the mutual porting and development initiatives, a 
full service and support offering also represents a key component in 
the Digital-Baan partnership. Digital's Services Division has solid 
experience and service capabilities on both NT and UNIX in 
multiplatform computing environments. 

"Digital and Baan have unique strengths that integrate well," said 
Mike Gallup, vice president of Digital's worldwide marketing. "Baan 
enjoys recognized expertise as an innovative developer of business 
application software, and Digital's Alpha platform delivers the 
highest level of scalability, flexibility and price/performance in 
the industry today. This partnership will deliver solutions to our 
customers that are comprehensive as well as cost-effective." 

"We are delighted to see this level of investment and commitment 
from Digital," said Doug Sallen, vice-president of corporate 
marketing for The Baan Company. "The industry-wide shift to Windows 
NT-based solutions has dramatically changed the landscape of 
computing. Digital has established a unique strategic alliance with 
Microsoft, and optimizing our development efforts on the Digital 
Alpha/NT platform will assist us in providing customers the 
flexibility that is demanded in ERP application scenarios."

About The Baan Company
----------------------

The Baan Company (NASDAQ:BAANF; Amsterdam Stock Exchange:BAAN) is a 
leading provider of enterprise-wide business software applications 
and consulting services. The company offers the Baan family of 
integrated, open-systems based applications and tools developed for 
the client/server architecture.

