               Digital Launches TP Internet Server for
           Fast, Secure Enterprise Transaction Processing
                          Over the Internet

... Provides cost-effective, standards-based transaction processing 
            alternative to expensive private networks ...
                     Passes the "ACID" test ...

MAYNARD, Mass., July 3, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced the first "industrial strength" software solution that 
provides secure business-to-business transaction processing (TP), 
with full transaction integrity, using open, cost-effective Internet 
connections. This unique offering, called TP Internet Server, 
reinforces Digital's ability to solve customers' most complex, 
mission-critical business challenges.

     TP Internet Server integrates Digital's high-volume, three-tier 
ACMSxp TP monitor with leadership AltaVista Tunnel encryption 
technology. TP Internet Server will be available for Digital UNIX 
and Windows NT servers and will support Windows 95 and Windows NT 
clients. Configurations can be designed for OpenVMS environments by 
exploiting the affinity between Windows NT and OpenVMS.  

     TP Internet Server simplifies operations between 
manufacturers/distributors and their suppliers and strengthens the 
coordination between headquarters and branch office operations. 
The product is designed for applications such as financial services, 
insurance claims processing, order processing, inventory control, 
and distribution, which are ideally suited to Internet access and 
require both robust security and transaction and data integrity.

     "To exploit the enormous potential for transacting business 
over the Internet, our customers demand bullet-proof transaction 
integrity and data security," said Steve Jenkins, Digital vice 
president of Commercial Software Products. "Enterprise transaction 
processing over the Internet is, for the first time, a choice that 
can be made without sacrificing the safeguards customers expect from 
serious transactional systems."

     According to Keith Steva, senior vice president of Digi-Key, an 
electronics distribution company in Thief River Falls, Minn., 
"Digital's TP Internet Server will enable Digi-Key to grow the 
business by enhancing customer service for both new and current 
customers while maintaining the business operations integrity our 
business demands. Now we feel comfortable exploiting the power, 
flexibility, and affordability of the Internet to reach out to new 
customers and partners and develop new services."

Integrating Critical Line-of-Business Applications

     Jim Johnson, chairman and founder of The Standish Group, 
Dennis, Mass., a leading market research and advisory firm for the 
electronic commerce marketplace, said, "Digital's TP Internet 
Server, with its capability to deliver secure transaction processing 
over the Internet, will provide a new dimension of functionality for 
corporate Intranet and electronic commerce."

     TP Internet Server passes the "ACID" test for industrial-
strength transaction processing: Atomicity, requiring that either 
all or none of a transaction's pieces are committed; Consistency, or 
data validity; Isolation, requiring that each transaction is 
isolated from any other transaction while it is in process; and 
Durability, requiring that committed data is saved by the system, 
even in the event of failure.

     Aluizio Borges, managing director, Banco Bradesco S.A., 
Brazil's largest bank, said, "Digital's solution for Transaction 
Processing over the Internet combines features that guarantee a 
secure use of the Internet together with data integrity. Bradesco 
will evaluate it to be used in the Remote Banking applications." 

     TP Internet Server integrates the robust, open power of ACMSxp 
and the firewall- and application-independence of AltaVista Tunnel.  
This assures the capabilities businesses need in order to develop, 
deploy, and manage three-tier client/server TP applications 
effectively and productively across multiple Internet- and 
Intranet-based platforms. 

     ACMSxp incorporates industry standards for data communications 
such as DCE, SPIRIT, and X/Open, providing portability and inter-
operability of applications across multiple operating environments. 
It also complies with the XA standard, permitting the use of 
multiple databases and interoperation with other transaction 
systems.

     Whether developing new applications or re-engineering current 
applications, ACMSxp applications are are easy and fast to build 
using a simplified high level language. Digital Application 
Generator, a development tool, is also available to rapidly generate 
complete client-server ACMSxp applications. ACMSxp provides high 
scalability, high availability features such as failover, 
application management and control, such as load balancing, and 
two-phase commit for transaction and data integrity. 

     AltaVista Tunnel products, in Workgroup Edition or Personal 
Edition, enable servers and PCs to connect to private networks via 
the Internet.  This allows companies to replace or extend their 
leased communications lines and modem banks with bandwidth supplied 
by Internet Service Providers, reducing network management and 
operation costs while providing the security and throughput needed 
for business-critical transactions. 

     AltaVista Tunnel enables information to be transmitted from one 
computer to another over a public network as if the two were 
connected by a single secure wire. After authentication of the 
tunnel client and the tunnel server, information is encrypted and 
sent across the Internet as unrecognizable information. Once the 
information reaches its final destination, the packets are decrypted 
and reconstituted into a readable form.

Pricing and Availability

     TP Internet Server is available in August and priced beginning 
at $6,400 for Windows NT server systems and $14,200 for Digital UNIX 
systems. Client software starts at $192. For more information, 
please go to the World Wide Web site http://www.software.digital.com

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
