                SAP Certifies Digital's Process Data
                         Acquisition System

MAYNARD, Mass., July 10, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
announced today that its Process Data Acquisition System (PDAS) 
software has been certified by SAP AG for the SAP PI-PCS interface.  
The certification was obtained last month at the SAP AG facility in 
Walldorf, Germany.  Certification was obtained for Digital UNIX, 
Intel Windows NT, Alpha Windows NT, and HP-UX (UNIX) releases of the 
PDAS software.  

     PDAS is a plant floor integration software that was developed 
as a complementary solution to SAP R/3 Production Planning for 
Process Industries (PP-PI) module.  PDAS facilitates the integration 
between manufacturing applications, plant equipment, and the SAP R/3 
PP-PI module, closing the gap between the event-based world of 
process control and the transaction-based world of R/3.  PDAS 
concepts are based on the ISA SP88 Standard for Process Control 
Systems.

     PDAS was the first industry software to be certified by SAP to 
the PP-PI standard in October 1994. The current certification 
updates the 1994 certification to Version 3 of R/3.

     According to John Egolf, Digital's PDAS Program Manager, "The 
open, flexible architecture of PDAS gives plant managers the ability 
to utilize existing PLCs and control equipment to easily integrate 
the real-time plant floor data into SAP R/3.  This real-time, 
corporate-wide access to critical information helps differentiate 
PDAS customers from their competitors by enabling them to satisfy 
their customer base in terms of price, delivery, and quality."

PDAS software operates in a distributed processing environment and 
features:

     - 	Certified interface, by SAP, to PP-PI

     - 	Collection, management, filtering and distribution of plant data

     - 	Automatic notification of significant and critical events in a plant

     - 	Dynamic configuration of data-collection, parameters, and   
        data-filtering requirements from recipes

     - 	Integration to Laboratory Information and Management Systems (LIMS)

     - 	Integration to process visualization and historian applications

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a worldwide SAP Hardware 
Partner and a Logo Partner, providing SAP services in many countries 
around the world.  Through a network of SAP Expertise Centers and 
Competency Centers, Digital has helped implement solutions at more 
than 800 SAP customer locations in more than 40 countries.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
