        Spire Technologies and Digital Equipment Corporation
               Partner on Capacity Planning Solutions

... Critical performance management and capacity planning functions
       to work in heterogeneous, client/server environment ...

OREM, Utah -- Spire Technologies, Inc. and Digital Equipment 
Corporation today announced the formation of a joint technology 
development and marketing relationship that will lead the UNIX 
market for client/server performance monitoring, management, and 
capacity planning solutions.  

Under the terms of the agreement, Spire is providing Digital with 
the API (Application Programming Interface) to connect Digital's 
POLYCENTER Capacity Planning product with the data collection 
modules from OpenAviator, Spire's resource availability tool.  This 
interactive connectivity provides for integrated system evaluation, 
planning, and management regardless of the user's computing 
environment configurations.

"OpenAviator collects performance data from over 18 different UNIX 
systems," said Gary Godfrey, President of Spire Technologies. "As a 
result of this new agreement, this data can now be read and 
understood by Digital's POLYCENTER Capacity Planner for projecting 
what-if scenarios across heterogeneous computing environments.  
Combined, these tools provides managers of multi-vendor UNIX 
client/server environments with a comprehensive planning and 
management solution."

OpenAviator's GUI interface provides IT managers, application 
developers, and LAN managers with comprehensive on-line resource 
monitoring, background trending, alarm management, parametric data 
collection, and customizable data collection engines.  Open Aviator 
monitors and manages critical data from all major UNIX and NT 
operating systems, Oracle, Ingres, Informix, Sybase, and Unify 
databases; and all third-party software applications.

"With this agreement, customers will use one set of tools to manage 
system performance and plan system and network capacity," said 
Kannankote Srikanth, Vice President of Digital's Network and Systems 
Integration business.  "This will result in a more holistic approach 
to planning UNIX systems, saving time and money while increasing 
end-user productivity."

Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions, from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software, and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.

Spire Technologies has been serving the mid-range computing 
environment since 1986.  In addition to OpenAviator, Spire 
Technologies is the developer and worldwide distributor of Corel 
WordPerfect for Digital UNIX and Digital's OpenVMS environments.  
Spire also provides organizations with leading System Management 
tools, Internet and Intranet Security, Backup and Restore 
capabilities, User Training and Support solutions, Network 
Management tools, and Office Automation software.  Spire is also 
an authorized Business Partner and PATHWORKS reseller for Digital 
Equipment Corporation.  
