COMDEX/Canada '96, TORONTO, July 11, 1996 - Digital Equipment of 
Canada today received The Computer Paper's Best of COMDEX/Canada 
Award, Best New Notebook category, for its HiNote Ultra II series of 
notebooks. 

The Digital HiNote Ultra II tied with Texas Instruments 6000 Series 
of notebooks in The Computer Paper's Best New Notebook category. 
"There were so many hot hew notebooks at the show, it was difficult 
to name just one...so we named two.  The Digital HiNote Ultra II and 
the Texas Instruments 6000 series notebooks both appealed to our 
editors, narrowly edging out other great new portables," stated The 
Computer Paper in a news release issued earlier today. 

"We are delighted that our HiNote Notebooks have been recognized in 
this way", said Digital's director of communications, Ron 
Catcheside. "Trade shows, like COMDEX, are an excellent place for 
leading-edge companies to display their technology. This year's 
COMDEX continues with the tradition of recognizing Digital for its 
product excellence." 

Digital's HiNote Ultra II is a line of high-end portable computers 
that delivers advanced features, performance and maximum portability 
with the industry's thinnest, lightest notebook designs. The timing 
of this release corresponds with the today's introduction of 
Digital's enhanced line of HiNote notebooks which feature 11.3-inch 
SVGA color displays, 133MHz Intel Pentium processors and 6X-speed 
CD-ROM drive enhancements.  The company said it plans to make 
additional models with 11.3-inch displays available this summer that 
will include faster mobile Pentium processor technology from Intel 
Corporation. 

Digital's HiNote family is targeted at customers from the small 
office business user to sophisticated, large business mobile 
professionals. Estimated street pricing for the HiNote Ultra II 
series starts at CDN $5,489. 

