BURLINGTON, Mass - July 15, 1996 - Cognos (NASDAQ;COGNF:TSE;CSN) and 
Digital Equipment Corp (NASDAQ;DEC) today announced an agreement 
under which Digital will resell and support Impromptu and PowerPlay, 
Cognos' award-winning business intelligence tools.  The worldwide 
strategic agreement builds on Cognos' commitment to supporting Alpha 
Warehouse, Digital's data warehousing initiative that helps 
customers turn data into competitive information.

Based on the agreement, Cognos will train and certify Digital 
systems integration professionals to design and implement data 
warehouse solutions using Impromptu and PowerPlay as the front end 
tools.  In addition to Alpha Warehouse, Digital will also recommend 
Cognos products for use as data access and reporting tools over 
corporate Intranets.    

Impromptu, Cognos' market leading query and reporting front end,
complements Digital's Alpha systems by providing access to corporate 
data stored in data warehouses and in business systems, such as SAP 
R/3.  PowerPlay, the world's most popular OLAP tools, provide quick 
and easy data analysis, drilling down on the details of the 
business.

"Cognos and Digital have worked well together as business partners," 
Alan Rottenberg, Cognos' senior vice president, Business 
Intelligence products said. "Together we ensure that customers 
receive the best possible integration, service and support for their 
business reporting and decision support solutions."

Kannankote Srikanth, Digital's vice president for Networks and 
Systems Integration Services, said that the partnership with Cognos 
is a key component in Digital's strategy for providing a 
comprehensive data warehouse solution.  "Coupling Impromptu and 
PowerPlay into the Alpha Warehouse solution empowers end users with 
direct access to corporate-wide information that is key to managing 
their business."

Alpha Warehouse is a complete, low-risk, flexible solution that 
leverages an organization's data assets for maximum competitive 
advantage.  It encompasses the industry's leading database vendors,
application tool developers, servers, storage, and networks, as well 
as the expertise to tie them all together. 

Digital Equipment Corp. is the world's leader in open client/server
solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.

Cognos is the global leader in providing business intelligence 
software to satisfy enterprise-wide data access and analysis needs.  
With over a quarter of a million seats in thousands of companies 
worldwide, PowerPlay and Impromptu consistently service the widest 
range of users across corporate, departmental, workgroup, personal 
and mobile applications.  The products support over 100 relational 
and OLAP data sources and are available in seven major languages.  
Cognos business intelligence products can be purchased from the 
company's regional offices and more than 450 resellers around the 
globe.

Cognos develops, markets and supports -- both directly and through 
resellers worldwide -- client/server tools for data access, data 
analysis and application development on a wide range of open and 
proprietary computing platforms.  Cognos is a publicly held company 
with dual headquarters in Ottawa, Canada and Burlington, MA.  
Cognos' World Wide Web address is http://www.cognos.com.
