        Digital Adds Oracle Database Support to Portfolio of
            High-Performance Storage Management Solutions

      ... Announces Plans to Integrate NetWorker for Windows NT
                    with Microsoft BackOffice ...

MAYNARD, Mass., July 16, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today
announced storage management software that lets users back up and 
restore multiple, distributed Oracle7 databases with the highest 
levels of performance, data protection and ease of use. Database 
Module for Oracle V1.0 works with Digital's NetWorker Save and 
Restore for Digital UNIX to offer customers more rapid and 
consistent backup and network-wide data protection than is available 
from Oracle7 alone.

     The company also announced that its family of NetWorker Save 
and Restore products, which offers the industry's broadest 
multi-platform support for high-performance storage management, will 
integrate fully with Microsoft's BackOffice suite for Windows NT.

     "Digital is significantly enhancing the distributed storage 
management capabilities available to our customers," said Laura 
Woodburn, vice president of Digital's Storage Business Segment. 
"Users of Oracle7 on Digital UNIX now have an automated, industrial-
strength backup-and-restore solution that maximizes data 
availability and peace of mind."

NetWorker Database Module for Oracle

     NetWorker Save and Restore for Digital UNIX provides high-
performance backup, recovery and archival services for multivendor 
systems in networked TCP/IP environments. The Database Module for 
Oracle extends the performance, functionality and reliability of 
NetWorker to the Oracle7 enterprise backup utility (EBU). The 
combination of NetWorker Database Module and EBU ensures database 
security and referential integrity, while providing consistent
enforcement of backup policies, automatic verification of backup 
operations and comprehensive media management. 

     NetWorker Database Module for Oracle allows parallel streaming 
of Oracle7 files at full speed, an ideal solution for large backup 
environments and high-availability systems with small backup 
windows. Backups can occur while the database is on-line and in use, 
minimizing impact on users. 

     NetWorker Database Module for Oracle is available immediately 
from Digital and its distribution partners, and is priced from 
US$6,000. 

NetWorker Enhancements to Include BackOffice Integration on Windows NT

     Digital delivers its NetWorker family of products through a 
long-term OEM relationship with Legato Systems, Inc. Through this 
and other agreements, Legato's NetWorker for UNIX has become the 
leading UNIX storage management solution.

     "The strength of the relationship between Legato and Digital 
has been critical in establishing this strong direction for 
NetWorker products for distributed client-server environments," said 
Gilbert Wai, senior vice president of product development at Legato 
Systems. "NetWorker integration with BackOffice on Windows NT will 
ensure that customers' requirements for sophisticated backup, 
restore, and archival continue to be met."

     Digital and Legato are jointly developing the integration of 
NetWorker for NT with Microsoft BackOffice. This integration will 
provide Windows NT users with a consistent, unified set of storage, 
system and network management tools that reduce administration 
complexity and costs. Planned availability for NetWorker integration 
with BackOffice on Alpha NT is early 1997.

     For more information about Digital's complete line of storage 
hardware and software products, call 1-800-STORWORK (1-800-786-7967) 
or visit http://www.storage.digital.com on the World Wide Web. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
