            INTERSOLV Delivers DataDirect Middleware for
                    Digital Equipment Corporation

      New DataDirect Windows NT ODBC Driver for Digital's Alpha
           Workstations and AlphaServer Enterprise Systems

ROCKVILLE, Maryland - July 17, 1996 - INTERSOLV (NASDAQ:  ISLI), the 
leader in applications enablement, today announced a new agreement 
with Digital Equipment Corporation to deliver the award-winning 
DataDirect ODBC technology for Digital's family of high-performance 
Alpha workstations and AlphaServers.  Through this strategic 
relationship, Digital Alpha platform developers are empowered to 
rapidly develop and deploy ODBC-compliant applications through the 
DataDirect middleware.

Under terms of the agreement, INTERSOLV will develop and deliver 
DataDirect Windows NT ODBC Drivers for Alpha workstations and 
AlphaServers, providing powerful data connectivity to Informix, 
Oracle, Sybase, Ingres and Microsoft SQL Server data sources.  As a 
strategic partner, Digital will provide INTERSOLV the technical and 
business development support required to bring the market-leading 
DataDirect ODBC Drivers to the high-performance Alpha platforms 
running Windows NT.

"The agreement that Digital has put in place with INTERSOLV is a 
comprehensive collaboration, particularly for those customers who 
require database independence on a Windows NT platform," said Mike 
Gallup, Digital's vice president of worldwide systems marketing.  
"Digital's Alpha architecture, with its speed and scalability, will 
drive INTERSOLV's high-performance data access products, supporting 
the critical business information needs of our mutual customers."

The Open Database Connectivity (ODBC) specification is the standard 
for database-independent data access.  ODBC allows developers to 
design applications based on a common API rather than a specific 
DBMS, thus creating applications that are easily portable from one 
DBMS to another.  The award-winning DataDirect Drivers from 
INTERSOLV provide the critical link to multiple data sources.

"With this agreement, INTERSOLV demonstrates our continued 
commitment to providing customers powerful data connectivity 
solutions for developing robust, database-independent applications 
across all the popular operating systems and servers," said Ed 
Peters, vice president and general manager of DataDirect.  "By 
selecting INTERSOLV as their middleware partner, Digital offers 
their customers high-performance, flexible ODBC-based data 
connectivity."

Digital joins more than 60 existing DataDirect strategic partners 
whose products offer the benefit of cross-platform, rapid data 
access through the industry's most robust client and server 
middleware technology.  With more than one million customers 
worldwide, INTERSOLV DataDirect delivers high-performance data 
access to critical business information.

INTERSOLV DataDirect

With high-performance data access products that span more than 35 
databases and more than 130 combinations of cross-platform data 
access, INTERSOLV's award-winning technology empowers developers to 
rapidly develop and deploy ODBC-compliant applications.  Providing 
the most comprehensive combination of platforms and databases 
available, INTERSOLV's high-performance DataDirect Drivers access 
more databases than any other vendor and support the most popular 
client/server operating systems - Windows, Windows NT, Windows 95, 
OS/2, Macintosh, HP-UX, IBM AIX and Solaris - making DataDirect the 
industry's leading cross-platform ODBC solution.  More than one 
million customers use DataDirect to achieve transparent data access.  
INTERSOLV has attracted DataDirect partnerships with leading 
independent software vendors, including Borland, Computer 
Associates, IBM, Informix, JavaSoft, Lotus, Microsoft, Oracle, 
Progress and Sybase.

Pricing and Availability

The DataDirect Windows NT ODBC Driver for Digital's family of Alpha 
workstations and AlphaServers will be available by the end of the 
year for $99.  For more information, contact INTERSOLV at (800) 
876-3101.

