             Digital Announces PATHWORKS Advances Server

         Provides Seamless Windows NT Integration With UNIX

MAYNARD, Mass., July 22, 1996 --- Digital Equipment Corporation. the 
leading provider of enterprise Windows NT solutions, today announced 
the release of its PATHWORKS V6.0 for Digital UNIX (Advanced Server) 
which provides Windows NT networking services on Digital UNIX.

     PATHWORKS V6.0 is the connectivity solution for Windows and 
Windows NT sites that need the scalability and reliability of 
Digital UNIX for mission-critical applications and enterprise 
databases.

     It allows PC users to participate as full players in an 
enterprise-wide client/server environment, and is the solution for 
existing Digital UNIX customers who are now also implementing 
Windows NT solutions.

     With its PATHWORKS family of products, Digital has supported 
the broadest set of PC clients, servers, network operating systems, 
network transports and protocols.

     With PATHWORKS V6.0, PC users are now able to take advantage of 
the built-in application availability, data integrity and security 
features offered by mid-size, large, and clustered Digital UNIX 
Alpha systems. 

     "As the industry leader in both 64-bit clustered UNIX computing 
and in integrating Windows NT throughout the enterprise, Digital is 
in a unique position to enable customers to exploit the power of 
64-bit computing from their Windows clients and Windows NT clients 
and servers. With the release of PATHWORKS V6.0, Digital further 
improves customers' competitiveness by exploiting the technology 
advances of the Windows NT Server and Digital UNIX in productivity, 
security, and scalability for tighter coupling of their PC and UNIX 
computing environments," said Don Harbert, vice president of 
Digital's UNIX business segment.

     "With this new release, PCs are now able to take advantage of 
Digital's UNIX TruCluster Software, and the world's most scalable 
64-bit computing architecture," Harbert noted.

     As more and more businesses implement Windows NT solutions, 
they are faced with the challenge of integrating these solutions 
into their environment. PATHWORKS V6.0 provides seamless access to 
data and resources whether they operate on the Windows NT, NetWare, 
or Digital UNIX operating systems. 

     PATHWORKS V6.0 also provides server-to-server connectivity 
between Digital UNIX and Windows NT, allowing Digital UNIX to be a 
peer in a Windows NT environment.

     PATHWORKS V6.0 enables customers who are familiar with the 
Microsoft Windows NT management and administrative tools to use them 
to manage their server environment. PATHWORKS V6.0 supports Windows 
NT management RPCs (remote procedure calls) allowing PATHWORKS 
users, file shares, printers, and events to be manageable from an NT 
system. Windows NT security features are also included in this new 
release.

     Digital's PATHWORKS V6.0 for Digital UNIX (Advanced Server) is 
shipping today worldwide. It offers out-of-the-box desktop 
connectivity for Windows NT, Windows 95, Windows for Workgroups 
V3.11, and any other standard LAN manager client.

     This new PATHWORKS V6.0 Advanced Server is available for 
Digital's UNIX V4.0, and any client licensed to connect to PATHWORKS 
V5.0 server is automatically licensed to connect to the new 
PATHWORKS V6.0 Advanced Server.

     Flexible licensing options are available, including both 
client-based licensing and server-based licensing. Special pricing 
is in effect until September 30, 1996, ranging from $990 for 10 
users through $18,000 for 250 users.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
