           AltaVista Search for Windows 95 and Windows NT
          Preview Software Available on the World Wide Web

...AltaVista Search extended from the public Web to private PCs...

MAYNARD, Mass., July 23, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today
announced that a free preview version of AltaVista Search for 32-bit
Windows PCs is now available for public downloading at
http://altavista.software.digital.com on the World Wide Web.  With 
this release, AltaVista extends its powerful search and indexing 
capabilities to personal PCs, making the task of finding documents 
on Windows 95 and Windows NT laptops, desktops and workstations as 
fast and easy as searching the World Wide Web.  AltaVista Search My 
Computer Private eXtension (pX) uses the same proven technology that 
drives AltaVista, the Internet's award-winning search service, which 
now handles over 15 million inquires a day.

     "The exploding growth of the Internet and the rapidly expanding 
use of email and electronic documents often overpowers our ability 
to find the critical data we need," said Ilene H. Lang, vice 
president of Digital's Internet Software Business Unit.  "With 
AltaVista Search, we return the power to quickly and accurately 
discover information to the individual.  The AltaVista Search 
Private eXtension products and the AltaVista Search public service 
on the Web are the keys to our concept of OnSite Knowledge -- 
location-independent access to the information people need, where 
and when they need it.  If it's out there, AltaVista Search can find 
it."
     AltaVista Search My Computer pX automatically builds a full 
word index of all HTML documents and over 140 popular file types on 
a PC and local network.   Within seconds, users navigating with the 
familiar AltaVista Search interface can find all documents on their 
local drives and shared networked drives that contain a selected 
search term.  Clicking on a document in the AltaVista index will 
automatically open the document and launch the application that 
created it.  Included among the many applications supported by 
AltaVista Search are Microsoft Word, Excel and Power Point, and 
Microsoft Exchange and Eudora email.

     AltaVista Search Private eXtensions give the Internet/Intranet 
user a single tool to search any and all information resources 
within their realm of access.  A single interface allows users to 
seamlessly search from their PC to the entire World Wide Web and 
back again without having to change applications or learn new 
interfaces.  AltaVista Search Private eXtensions are scaleable to 
fit a user's needs, searching for information on a single floppy 
disk to terabyte-size storage arrays.

     Further information on these products is available on the 
AltaVista Software World Wide Web site, located at
http://altavista.software.digital.com, or by calling 800-336-7890.

     AltaVista software solutions from Digital provide high 
performance Internet connectivity to help cyberworkers quickly find 
useful information, easily communicate and collaborate over secure 
virtual networks. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.  
