                    Digital Equipment Corporation Announces Plan
             to Repurchase Up to 10 Million Shares of Its Common Stock
        
    MAYNARD, Mass., July 30, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
    (NYSE:DEC) today announced that its Board of Directors has authorized 
    the repurchase, as conditions warrant, of up to 10 million shares of 
    the company's common stock. The shares will be used for employee 
    stock plans.
    
    	 The total number of shares of common stock outstanding, as of 
    June 29, 1996, was 155,504,284 shares.
    
    	"We have confidence in the underlying strengths of the company," 
    said Digital Chairman Robert B. Palmer. "This is an opportunity to 
    enhance shareholder value."
    
    	Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open 
    client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
    worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
    storage, networking, software and services, together with 
    industry-focused solutions from business partners, help organizations 
    compete and win in today's global marketplace.
    
