           PeopleSoft Announces Online Performance Benchmark 
                    for Enterprise Financials 

       ...Results Show Fast Response For 2,300 Concurrent Users 
          on Digital's 64-Bit AlphaServer 8400 Platform...

     PLEASANTON, CA, July 29, 1996 -- PeopleSoft, Inc., (NASDAQ: PSFT), a 
leading provider of client/server business software, today announced that 
it has completed, in conjunction with Digital Equipment Corporation, a 
performance benchmark study to measure online performance of integrated 
PeopleSoft Financial application software on a Digital AlphaServer 8400 
enterprise system running a 64-bit Digital Unix and the 64-bit Oracle 7 
relational database. 

     The results of this benchmark clearly demonstrate that the combination 
of PeopleSoft Financials and Digital's 64-bit Very Large Memory (VLM64)
technology provides leadership performance and scalability, enabling more
users to achieve better response times, with high average update and 
retrieve rates and stable response times.

     Specifically, the benchmark study results demonstrate that PeopleSoft
Financials 5.01 processed online operations, representing 13 business
processes, at average overall update and retrieve rates of two and a half
seconds each.  The configuration maintained consistent response times as 
the number of concurrent users varied from one to 2,300.

      "This benchmark demonstrates that the combination of PeopleSoft, 
Digital and Oracle 7 exceeds the enterprise level demands of our customers 
and prospects," said Rick Bergquist, vice president of technology at 
PeopleSoft.  "This powerful combination supports the high concurrent user 
volumes and very large databases typical of large enterprises today and in 
the future."

      "PeopleSoft and Digital have unique strengths that complement each 
other.  Programs such as the PeopleSoft Performance Engineering Program 
enable us to jointly bring predictable, high performance solutions to 
customer," said Pauline Nist, vice president of Digital's AlphaServer 
Business Segment.  

      "This benchmark study demonstrates the proven performance 
capabilities of Digital's AlphaServer systems," Nist added.  "With its 
64-bit Alpha architecture, 64-bit operating systems, 64-bit databases, and 
leading applications such as PeopleSoft, Digital stands alone in its 
ability to provide a complete 64-bit solution. As a result, the AlphaServer 
has a unique ability to support the high-performance transaction, 
throughput, and user loads required for enterprise solutions."

Benchmark Details

     The benchmark study was performed using a PeopleSoft Online Benchmark 
Kit on an AlphaServer 8400 system configured with 8 CPUs and more than 6 
gigabytes of memory, at the  PeopleSoft Performance Laboratory at the 
company's headquarters in Pleasanton, Calif. The study, a joint effort 
using engineers and other resources from both PeopleSoft and Digital, was 
designed to demonstrate the performance and scalability of complex 
financial transactions, large numbers of concurrent users, and high 
business process throughput of PeopleSoft on the Digital AlphaServer 8400 
system.  This study was performed on version 5.01 of PeopleSoft General 
Ledger, Accounts Payable, Accounts Receivable, Asset Management and nVision 
reporting.  

      Digital's AlphaServer family of systems is the industry's only 
complete line of tested, proven and mature high performance 64-bit RISC 
servers, ranging from the AlphaServer 8400 enterprise server, to the 
AlphaServer 4100 midrange server, to the AlphaServer 2100 departmental 
server. Digital delivers price/performance platform leadership for all 
PeopleSoft solutions.

     	To ensure that the test modeled the requirements of large, complex 
organizations, the benchmark kit from PeopleSoft was designed with input 
from Ford Motor Company, USAA Insurance, UPS, Corning, Inc., and McDonnell 
Douglas.

     The study tested 13 separate business processes, each defined as a 
series of panels and dialog boxes that guide a user through an entire 
procedure, such as journal or ledger entry, applying payments, maintaining 
customers, asset inquiry, and nVision reporting.  

     Some of the business processes tested included multiple functions. 
Business processes were tested in order to measure realistic business 
performance measures rather than the traditional screen-to-screen 
transaction testing.  

     Industry analysts and members of the press may request copies of 
PeopleSoft Performance Reports from The Horn Group (see contact information 
above).

PeopleSoft Benchmark Kits

     PeopleSoft benchmarks kit include application software, data for 
standard performance benchmarks, database expansion tools, and standard 
documentation templates to capture benchmark information. These kits 
facilitate partner and customer performance engineering and benchmark 
efforts using standard testing methods and datasets. Customer 
implementation teams also use benchmark kits to tune their PeopleSoft 
applications using their own hardware configuration and customized data 
compositions very early in the implementation lifecycle. 

     PeopleSoft has also developed performance tests consisting of 
realistic database and transaction data expanded to small, medium, large, 
and very large volumes. Each model is developed using information collected 
from PeopleSoft's customer base. These standard performance models are used 
to perform all standard benchmarks. 

PeopleSoft Performance Engineering Program

     This benchmark study was conducted under the PeopleSoft Performance
Engineering Program was established late last year to assist PeopleSoft
customers to achieve optimal enterprise-level performance capabilities. 
Conducted in conjunction with PeopleSoft platform partners and customers, 
the performance benchmark studies will provide customers with information
to assist them in determining their ideal software and hardware 
requirements. 

     Numerous studies have been completed thus far and results are 
available in the program's performance information repository. This 
information is also being used to further improve performance in future 
releases of PeopleSoft products.  The repository includes a series of 
performance benchmark papers, published by PeopleSoft in conjunction with 
its platform partners and customers, that show high performance and 
scalability with PeopleSoft products in various hardware and database 
environments. Other elements of the program include the benchmark kits and 
a performance laboratory. 

About PeopleSoft 

     PeopleSoft Inc. (NASDAQ: PSFT) was established in 1987 to provide 
innovative software solutions that meet the changing business needs of 
enterprises worldwide.  A client/server applications pioneer and market 
share leader, PeopleSoft develops, markets, and supports a complete suite 
of enterprise solutions for accounting, materials management, distribution, 
manufacturing, human resources.  With more than 1000 customers around the 
world, the company has been recognized for both its award-winning customer 
service and remarkable growth. 

     PeopleSoft was listed by Fortune Magazine as one of the fastest 
growing companies in America in 1995.  PeopleSoft product and service 
information is located on the World Wide Web at http://www.peoplesoft.com.

About Digital Equipment Corp. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated worldwide 
information systems. Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, storage, 
networking, software and services, together with industry-focused solutions 
from business partners, help organizations compete and win in today's 
global marketplace.
